# `fj` CLI — Forgejo

Forgejo's CLI (`fj`) is installed via Homebrew as a standalone binary. It auto-detects the remote host from the git remote in the current directory.

## Basic usage

```bash
# Search issues
fj issue search [query]

# Create a PR
fj pr create "WIP: title" [--body "..."] [--base main]

# Check CI status
fj actions tasks
```

## Remote detection

`fj` reads the git remote URL from the current repo. Local Cove remotes use `git@forgejo-localhost:cristos/repo.git` — the `forgejo-localhost` SSH config alias handles routing to `localhost:2222` with the correct SSH key.

## HTTPS auth

`cove up` caches a persistent API token (`cove-push`) in git's credential helper so `fj` can push over HTTPS without prompting.

## PR comments

```bash
# View all comments on a PR
fj pr view <PR#> comments

# View a specific comment by index (0-indexed)
fj pr view <PR#> comment <IDX>
```

